<title>FRANCE: Jospin hopes for success in Amsterdam.</title>
<headline>Jospin hopes for success in Amsterdam.</headline>
<dateline>POITIERS, France 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Lionel Jospin told German Chancellor Helmut Kohl that he hoped for an agreement on the stability pact in Amsterdam, provided that his proposals on jobs and policy coordination are taken into account, a source close to the prime minister said.</p>
<p>The source added that &quot;nothing has been ruled out, nothing has been concluded&quot; at the Franco-German summit here.  </p>
<p>The source said it was &quot;absurd to speak of either failure or success at the Poitiers summit. It was an important step and one that allowed some progress&quot;.</p>
<p>A German source said Kohl expressed his understanding of the new French demands during the talks but reaffirmed his desire to avoid a case that these entail additional spending.</p>
<p>A news conference on the summit was scheduled to begin around 1600 local time (1400 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
